cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QEHT in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "QEHT: QGIS Engineering Hydrology Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  An open-source QGIS Processing plugin for DEM-based engineering hydrology
  along road corridors. It conditions the DEM, resolves flats, builds the
  drainage network, delineates catchments, finds crossings, and computes
  catchment characteristics, soils and erosion screening, and DEM
  uncertainty. Results go into a documented design-hydrology exchange
  package. The numerical core is NumPy/GDAL, runs independently of QGIS,
  and is validated against a reference GIS platform's hydrology toolset.
